# Source is always diffable. A fixture generator legitimately embeds control
# characters as test payload, and a single stray NUL byte in the first 8 KiB is
# enough for git's heuristic to classify the whole file binary — which silently
# hides its diffs from review. Source files declare themselves text so that
# cannot happen; the escapes in the generator keep them out of the bytes anyway.
*.ts text diff
*.js text diff
*.mjs text diff

# Committed cross-language wire fixture: real frame bytes, never a text diff.
tests/fixtures/*.bin binary
